From 8261cc515787397380c36438cee0afafd9989d45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kostersitz <mkostersitz@mac.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:32:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] DisplayMask: match the stock semantics (rotation-0
 rects, app-visible hinge, gapless seam)

getBoundingRects() now always returns the hinge in rotation-0 physical coordinates and getBoundingRectsForRotation(r) maps it with the general
display-rotation transform (invalid rotations throw IllegalArgumentException), as the stock Duo class does. The mask is empty unless the hinge
intersects the app-visible area of the current rotation (single-panel postures, windows that do not cross the hinge, other devices). With the hinge
gap disabled (display exactly two panels wide) a 2 px virtual seam is reported. The arithmetic lives in HingeMath (no android.* classes) with a host
test in surface-sdk/boot/test. The visible-hinge decision is re-evaluated on every query because Microsoft Launcher holds an instance while the
posture changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

